Requirements:
- Create exactly one pytest test function named test_claim_{{ claim_slug }}.
- Include "import pytest".
- Add Given/When/Then as comments.
- If you cannot reliably call the real function due to unknown fixtures, write a "contract test":
  - import the module
  - assert that the target symbol exists (hasattr)
  - and assert the described exception behavior with a minimal call if possible
- Prefer testing observable outcomes: no exception raised, exception raised, return value, invariants.
- Keep runtime fast and deterministic.
